# The upstream-ownership ratchet manifest is written by a custom serializer
# (serializeManifest in src/upstream-ratchet.ts): one line per file entry,
# sorted by path, so two PRs regenerating it conflict only on paths they both
# touched. Prettier would reflow all 959 entries back into an indented shape and
# turn the file into a merge minefield. Regenerate it, never format it:
#   pnpm run ratchet:report -- --write
src/upstream-ratchet.json

# The vendored worker policy is generated twice from one render
# (renderWorkerPolicyModule in src/workflow-agent-vendor.ts) — once here and
# once into container/agent-runner/src/, which is a separate Bun tree prettier
# never sees. Both copies are fingerprinted under ONE hash, so the two files
# must be the same bytes. The renderer encodes its values with JSON.stringify
# (double quotes) because a generator writes structured output through an
# encoder, never a quote-pasting template; formatting this copy to singleQuote
# breaks the byte-identity and every drift test that rests on it. Regenerate it,
# never format it:
#   pnpm exec tsx scripts/vendor-workflow-agent.ts
src/worker-policy.vendored.ts
